From 74c315eed983674505fe95b3d47101363b9d5a2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaxdad <atxhxag@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:51:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] feat(web): open the graphics pipeline and hand H.264 to
 JavaScript

Two session builder extensions:

- `enable_egfx` advertises the Graphics Pipeline (MS-RDPEGFX) and opens its
  dynamic channel. Without an H.264 decoder no AVC capability set is
  advertised and the server picks among the other codecs.
- `h264_frame_callback`, with `enable_egfx`, adds a decoder that presents
  frames itself: each H.264 picture is called back as
  `(data, regions, surfaceId)`, with `data` an Annex B access unit and
  `regions` packing `[x, y, width, height]` per region (none means decode
  only), so the page can decode it, for example with WebCodecs, and draw it
  onto the canvas.

A `ResetGraphics` resizes the decoded image without the
Deactivation-Reactivation Sequence, so the canvas now follows the image's
size before each draw and before H.264 frames go to the callback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
